   $q$Why does the author end the story with Rafael smiling on the bus?$q$, $q$[{"text":"To show that Rafael is secretly glad he will not have to defend the record.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"To show that the official's thank you was the only thing Rafael wanted.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"To show that doing the right thing brought him a kind of pride that a record could not.","is_correct":true},{"text":"To suggest that Rafael expects to break the record at the next meet.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$To show that doing the right thing brought him a kind of pride that a record could not.$q$, $q$After his coach calls his honesty "the best thing I saw all day," Rafael smiles despite losing the record, which completes the theme. The story never mentions a future meet, so that choice adds an idea not in the text.$q$, 'draft', '5b05a701-5743-55e6-85f7-85d5889a54ef')
