   $q$How does the scene on the porch help develop the theme?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It shows that Grandpa Kwame wants to move back to his old farm.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It explains why Grandpa Kwame kept closing the video call by accident.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-cause-effect"},{"text":"It reverses the roles, so the grandfather becomes the teacher and Kofi the learner.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It shows that Kofi and his grandfather would rather drink lemonade than work.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It reverses the roles, so the grandfather becomes the teacher and Kofi the learner.$q$, $q$On the porch, Kofi is the one "asking question after question," which flips who is teaching. The lemonade break is the setting for the scene, not its meaning.$q$, 'draft', '270a4759-817f-556e-8b32-3e16408a46b5')
