   $q$The prefix in- can mean "not," the root vis means "see," and the suffix -ible means "able to be." What does Grandma mean when she says the cells are "invisible without help"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They are hidden inside the onion forever","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"They are too delicate to be touched safely","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-root-clues"},{"text":"They cannot be seen without a tool to help","is_correct":true},{"text":"They are easy to see with the eyes alone","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They cannot be seen without a tool to help$q$, $q$Invisible means "not able to be seen," and "without help" tells us the cells need a microscope. The answer that they are easy to see ignores the prefix in-, which means "not."$q$, 'draft', 'b30167b8-e836-5642-a884-a4c4479be157')
