   $q$The prefix e- means "out," and the Latin root ject means "throw." What do the pods do when they "eject the seeds"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They throw the seeds out with force","is_correct":true},{"text":"They pull the seeds back inside","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"They wrap the seeds in thick shells","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"They let the seeds dry out slowly","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-root-clues"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They throw the seeds out with force$q$, $q$Eject means "throw out," and the passage says the pods burst open and the seeds land several feet away. Drying out happens before the pods burst, so it does not describe what eject means.$q$, 'draft', 'ddd97707-5194-5811-90cf-ed551eae73fa')
