   $q$The prefix dis- can mean "apart" or "in different directions," and the root spers means "scatter." What is seed "dispersal"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The growing of seeds into tall adult plants","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-cause-effect"},{"text":"The gathering of seeds into one large pile","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"The drying of seeds in the hot summer sun","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"The spreading of seeds to many different places","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The spreading of seeds to many different places$q$, $q$Dis plus spers means "scatter apart," and the passage defines dispersal as the spreading of seeds. Growing into adult plants may happen after dispersal, but it is a result, not the meaning of the word.$q$, 'draft', 'ddd97707-5194-5811-90cf-ed551eae73fa')
