  ('cfb28935-4db7-53f0-91ca-54fac0ce1bf6', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g6-word-parts'), null, 'medium',
   $q$The prefix pro- can mean "in front of," and the Latin root tect means "cover." What does the coconut's shell do when it "protects the seed"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It covers the seed and keeps it from harm","is_correct":true},{"text":"It breaks open to let salt water reach the seed","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"It pushes the seed toward a distant beach","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-similar-word"},{"text":"It feeds the seed while it floats at sea","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It covers the seed and keeps it from harm$q$, $q$Protect means "cover in front of," and the passage says the thick shell keeps salt water away from the seed inside. Letting salt water in is the opposite of what the shell does.$q$, 'draft', 'ddd97707-5194-5811-90cf-ed551eae73fa')
