   $q$What is the author's main claim in this passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Linwood Middle School has a better garden than Redfern does.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Redfern Middle School should start a composting program this fall.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Compost bins always smell bad and attract pests to schools.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-counterclaim"},{"text":"The garden club should enter more flowers in the county fair.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Redfern Middle School should start a composting program this fall.$q$, $q$The first paragraph says "Redfern should start a composting program," and the conclusion repeats it. The worry about smells and pests is the opposing view the author answers, not the author's claim.$q$, 'draft', '44f71698-e636-585c-aa57-1581e5df4808')
