   $q$Which statement best describes how the author treats the strengths of digital notes?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The author lists their strengths to show that digital notes are better for every student.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-position"},{"text":"The author accepts them as real and allows exceptions, yet still favors handwriting for understanding.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The author claims digital notes have no strengths and that students who type are lazy.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"},{"text":"The author mentions their strengths only to complain that typed notes are too long.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-purpose"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The author accepts them as real and allows exceptions, yet still favors handwriting for understanding.$q$, $q$The author writes "Digital notes do have real strengths" and says students who need a keyboard "should always have that choice," then returns to the narrower claim about understanding. The author never says digital notes are better for every student.$q$, 'draft', 'ad71e547-42c8-528d-83b3-7fbbb33d66e0')
