  ('3ed5c666-6ab8-5220-8617-03a97bac4c00', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g7-connections'), null, 'hard',
   $q$How does the railroad in the final paragraph relate to the earlier events in the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The railroad was built because the canal had become too crowded with boats carrying flour and grain.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Faster, cheaper travel helped the village grow, and the railroad moved that advantage to another town.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The railroad ended the village's farms, since trains could not carry wheat during the cold winter.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"The railroad shows that the canal was never truly important to the growth of Harlow Falls.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-purpose"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Faster, cheaper travel helped the village grow, and the railroad moved that advantage to another town.$q$, $q$The village grew because the canal made shipping easier, and it stopped growing when faster trains that ran all winter drew business twelve miles north. The passage says trains could run in winter, so the claim about winter is backwards.$q$, 'draft', '6ac60994-f493-539a-acd1-bc3548aa98b9')
