   $q$According to paragraph 1, what caused the coral at Sandal Reef to turn white?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Divers broke off pieces to hang on underwater frames.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-cause-effect"},{"text":"Warmer water stressed the coral and it lost its algae.","is_correct":true},{"text":"A storm knocked the coral over and buried it in sand.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-sequence"},{"text":"Fish ate the colorful outer layer of the coral away.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Warmer water stressed the coral and it lost its algae.$q$, $q$Paragraph 1 says warmer water stressed the coral, "causing it to lose the tiny algae that give it food and color." The storm happened later and damaged the frames, not the original reef.$q$, 'draft', '424826ed-e0dd-5dfd-b1b5-6d447c8dfab4')
