-- Passage rg7-context-clues-p02
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('b80fc266-6640-50bf-a499-c621f85aa0c9', 'rg7-context-clues-p02', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g7-context-clues'), null,
        '6-8', $q$The Bake Sale Box$q$, $q$Mateo Reyes had agreed to run the seventh-grade bake sale, and his cousin Priya Shah had agreed to keep the money box. Priya was famously frugal. She reused paper bags, packed her own lunch every day, and had saved her allowance for two years to buy a used bicycle.

On Saturday morning, the table was crowded with muffins, banana bread, and three trays of oatmeal cookies. Priya kept a tally on a sheet of notebook paper, adding a small mark each time someone bought something.

By ten o'clock, the line was long. By noon, the stack of cookies had dwindled to a few broken pieces, and only two muffins remained. Mateo realized they had baked far too little banana bread and far too many lemon bars. The lemon bars were a surplus: twenty extra bars that nobody seemed to want.

"We could cut the price in half," Mateo suggested.

Priya frowned at her notebook. She hated selling anything for less than it was worth. Still, she knew leftover lemon bars would not help the class trip fund. "Fine," she said begrudgingly, crossing out the old price with a sigh. "Half price. But only for the lemon bars."

Within twenty minutes, every bar was gone. When they counted the money, the total was higher than either of them had expected. Priya looked at the final number and allowed herself a small smile.$q$, 'draft')
