values ('917905a9-ad28-52e3-805e-808340ec919c', 'rg7-context-clues-p08', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g7-context-clues'), null,
        '6-8', $q$The First Picture$q$, $q$When the Haddad family moved into their new apartment, Samira thought it felt sparse. There was a couch, two chairs, and a kitchen table, but the walls were bare, and the shelves were empty. Her voice echoed when she talked.

Her old bedroom had been the opposite. It had been cluttered with books, art supplies, and stuffed animals piled in every corner. Her mother used to joke that she needed a map to find the floor.

Samira was reluctant to unpack. If she put her things away, it would mean this place was really home, and she was not ready for that. Each day, she pulled out only what she needed and left the other boxes taped shut.

One afternoon, her little brother Nabil found a box labeled "Samira: Photos." Before she could stop him, he had opened it. Inside were pictures of her old street, her best friend Jada, and the maple tree in their old backyard. Samira felt nostalgic, a warm but slightly sad longing for the days in those photographs.

Nabil held up a picture of the maple tree. "We could put this one on your wall," he said. "Then you'll have it here too."

Samira looked at the empty wall above her bed. Maybe the new room could accommodate a few of her old memories after all. She found some tape, and together they hung the first picture.$q$, 'draft')
