values
  ('72132775-2924-5782-86cd-ea032451a256', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g7-evidence-inference'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Which evidence best supports the claim that drafting saves energy?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Wind tunnel studies found a rider in the middle of a pack may need far less energy than a rider alone.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Young cyclists usually practice drafting slowly with a coach before a race.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-supporting-detail"},{"text":"Riders in a pack have a harder time seeing the road ahead of them.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-supporting-detail"},{"text":"Riders in long races line up close behind one another or ride in a large pack.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"describes-not-supports"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Wind tunnel studies found a rider in the middle of a pack may need far less energy than a rider alone.$q$, $q$The wind tunnel studies measured energy and found pack riders need less of it. The fact that riders line up describes what drafting looks like but does not prove that it saves energy.$q$, 'draft', 'b282c102-d8f5-538b-9475-b9d1ae229035')
