  ('a29ab669-69a2-538e-ab26-e9a29eb9dc1f', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g7-evidence-inference'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Which sentence best explains why young cyclists practice drafting with a coach first?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Riders must stay only inches apart, so a sudden brake or a wobble can cause a crash.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Drafting is one of the most important tactics in long-distance bicycle racing.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-supporting-detail"},{"text":"One rider leads for a short stretch, then moves aside and drops to the back of the line.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-supporting-detail"},{"text":"A team may protect its strongest rider by keeping her sheltered for most of the race.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-supporting-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Riders must stay only inches apart, so a sudden brake or a wobble can cause a crash.$q$, $q$The last paragraph lists the crash risk and then says "For these reasons" young riders practice with a coach. The sentence about taking turns explains how drafting works, not why it needs careful practice.$q$, 'draft', 'b282c102-d8f5-538b-9475-b9d1ae229035')
