   $q$According to the passage, what did the conservators do before they did any painting?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They coated the whole surface with a clear layer that blocks sunlight.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-sequence"},{"text":"They added new figures to the blank corner to suit modern tastes.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"They cleaned the wall quickly with strong chemicals to remove the dirt.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"They studied the wall, tested the paints and searched for the artist's sketches.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They studied the wall, tested the paints and searched for the artist's sketches.$q$, $q$Paragraph 2 says their first step "was not painting" and describes two weeks of study. The clear coating came last, after the work was finished.$q$, 'draft', '8d455f9d-ae93-5a51-8119-0094b90628c0')
