  ('1b2fa5e5-047f-5573-b9a8-72965f26c457', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g7-evidence-inference'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Which pair of details best supports the conclusion that the team tried to keep the mural true to the artist's original work?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They filled the cracks in the wall, and they coated the surface with a clear layer.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-supporting-detail"},{"text":"They matched each color beside the old paint, and they did not add figures or change colors.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Much of the mural had faded, and in one corner the paint had peeled away entirely.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"describes-problem-not-solution"},{"text":"The mural shows a river and a market, and it has covered the wall for forty years.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They matched each color beside the old paint, and they did not add figures or change colors.$q$, $q$Matching old colors and refusing to add or change anything both show the team staying faithful to the original. Filling cracks and coating the wall repair and protect the mural, but they do not show faithfulness to the artist's choices.$q$, 'draft', '8d455f9d-ae93-5a51-8119-0094b90628c0')
